---
import { ArrowRight, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import Feature from '../components/Feature.astro';
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import release from '../data/alpha-release.json';
import docs from '../data/docs-revision.json';

const matrix = `https://github.com/eugene-plexus/specs/blob/${docs.commit}/docs/support-matrix.md`;
---

<SiteLayout title="Workbench, a local AI chat app with memory and documents | Eugene Plexus" description="Workbench is a self-hosted, local AI chat app: notes it remembers, answers from your documents and folders with their sources, and MCP tools you approve call by call.">
  <div class="container product-page">
    <header class="product-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Workbench · {release.version}</p>
      <h1>Workbench, a local AI chat app</h1>
      <p class="lead" data-plain>Workbench is Eugene's own chat app. It remembers what you ask it to, answers from your documents with their sources, and runs tools you approve.</p>
      <p>v0.3.0 suggests notes from your chats, which become notes only when you keep them, and lets other apps that speak MCP search your own notes and documents through connections you create and revoke. Sign-in can use Google, Microsoft or OpenID Connect. MCP Apps, A2UI forms and AG-UI conversations remain limited to the <a href={`https://github.com/eugene-plexus/specs/blob/${docs.commit}/docs/design/workbench-ui-browser-v1.md`}>published protocol subsets</a>.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/guides/install-workbench">Install Workbench <ArrowRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/guides/workbench-documents">Ask about your documents <ArrowRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <Shot name="workbench-web-search" eager caption="A chat with web search on: every source, with its site." alt="A Workbench chat in the light theme. A local Qwen3.8 model answered a question about Eugene Plexus with web search on; under the answer, Sources (5 searches) lists eugeneplexus.com and the project's GitHub pages, each with its site. Search the web is ticked beside the message box." />

    <Feature id="memory" index="01" title="Notes it remembers between chats" guides={['workbench-memory']} lead={'Say "Remember that…" and Workbench keeps a note. The Memory page shows every note, exports them, and deletes for real.'}>
      <Fragment slot="shots">
        <Shot name="workbench-memory" alt="Workbench’s Memory page: three notes, such as The garden’s plots are 4 by 8 feet, each marked Fact or Preference with Edit, Pin and Delete, a count of tokens and notes in use, and an Add a note box." />
      </Fragment>
      <ul>
        <li>Each chat shows exactly what it sent the model.</li>
        <li>By default, a model outside your machines gets no notes until you choose <strong>Send for this chat</strong>.</li>
        <li>Each person's notes are their own.</li>
      </ul>
    </Feature>

    <Feature id="documents" index="02" title="Ask about a file you attach" lead="Attach a PDF, a Word file, Markdown, text, CSV, HTML or code, and any model answers from it. The answer names the files.">
      <Fragment slot="shots">
        <Shot name="workbench-document" alt="A Workbench chat with a four-page PDF attached and the question how often the compost bins are turned. The answer, Every Monday evening, names the file, and Sources lists the pages sent to the model and their size in tokens." />
      </Fragment>
    </Feature>

    <Feature id="saved-documents" index="03" title="Saved documents and folders" lead="Keep documents, or grant a folder that stays in step, and Workbench searches them by words and by meaning, citing passages by file and page." guides={['workbench-documents', 'run-search-models']} limits={['The sorter’s default Sort time (3 s) suits a GPU, where a question takes about 0.6 s, not a typical CPU, where it takes about 7 s. Its gain was measured on questions written for those documents.']}>
      <Fragment slot="shots">
        <Shot name="workbench-citation" alt="A Workbench answer from saved documents: the volunteer workday is the first Saturday of each month at 9 am, citing source 1. Sources lists three passages from two documents by file and pages, with the cited passage open and its matching words marked." />
      </Fragment>
      <ul>
        <li>When a fast local result sorter runs, it puts the best passages first.</li>
        <li>A granted folder is checked for new, edited, deleted and moved files every 10 minutes, or when you press <strong>Sync now</strong>.</li>
        <li>Searching by meaning uses a search model on your own machines, unless the owner allows one outside them.</li>
      </ul>
    </Feature>

    <Feature id="tools" index="04" title="Approve each tool call" guides={['workbench-tools']} lead="Add shared or local MCP servers and folder tools. Each call waits for your approval in the chat.">
      <Fragment slot="shots">
        <Shot name="workbench-approval" alt="A Workbench chat in which the model asked to call a tool named list_files on a documents folder server. The call shows Waiting for approval, its arguments, and Approve call and Decline buttons." />
      </Fragment>
      <ul>
        <li>Shared MCP servers for everyone, local servers the owner adds, and folders the owner grants to a named person.</li>
        <li>Each server's command or address, and each folder's path, has a Copy button.</li>
        <li>MCP sign-in (OAuth), resources and prompts are not supported yet.</li>
        <li>For tools on another of your computers, make it a <a href="/job-sites">Job Site</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </Feature>

    <Feature id="more" index="05" title="The rest of Workbench" lead="Answer versions, web search with its sources, screens for images, speech, transcription and video, and a chat that reads well on a phone.">
      <Fragment slot="shots">
        <figure class="scene">
          <img src="/scenes/eugene-sawing.svg" width="200" height="200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Eugene sawing a board at his workbench while sawdust falls: one of the short scenes Workbench shows while a model works." />
          <figcaption>While a model works, Eugene works at the bench.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <Shot name="workbench-phone" alt="Workbench on a phone-width screen: the answer about the volunteer workday, its three sources with the first marked Cited, and the message box with Attach, the model picker and Send." phone />
      </Fragment>
      <ul>
        <li>Answer versions: <strong>Try again</strong> writes a new version of an answer, and every version is kept.</li>
        <li>Web search shows each source's site, plus Google's Search Suggestions, unmodified, when Google searched.</li>
        <li>Search chat names, drafts per chat, dropped files and pasted images, and a full Markdown export.</li>
        <li>Thinking, then Writing the answer, with the backend's own live token count and speed when it reports them.</li>
        <li>While a model works, Eugene works at the bench in short scenes, and holds still for reduced motion.</li>
        <li>You sign in with Eugene, and each person added under People gets their own chats.</li>
      </ul>
    </Feature>

    <details class="checked">
      <summary>How we checked</summary>
      <p>Memory, documents, saved documents, folders and the sorter each ran with a real Workbench and llama.cpp on the processor, with a small model; a run on the owner's own install is still owed. Tools ran on GitHub's Windows and Ubuntu runners with real service accounts and a scripted model. The image, speech and video screens each ran live once with paid accounts; the owner's install has no such model, so they have not run there. <a href={matrix}>The support matrix</a> has each record. <ArrowUpRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></p>
    </details>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .product-page { max-width: 1100px; padding-block: 4rem; }
  .product-intro h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -.015em; margin-block: 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .lead { max-width: 720px; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--muted); }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem 1.75rem; margin-block: 1.75rem 2.5rem; }
  .product-page :global(.feature) { display: flow-root; }
  .scene { float: right; margin: 0 0 1rem 1.5rem; text-align: center; max-width: 200px; }
  .scene img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .scene figcaption { margin-top: .4rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .scene { float: none; margin: 1rem auto; } }
  .checked { clear: both; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: var(--panel-soft); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .checked summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .checked p { line-height: 1.7; }
  .checked a, .product-page :global(.feature-details-body a) { color: var(--accent-left); }
</style>
